  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "NgCoreTerminologyService"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition NgCoreTerminologyService</b></p><a name=\"NgCoreTerminologyService\"> </a><a name=\"hcNgCoreTerminologyService\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: NgCoreTerminologyService </b></td><td>Nigeria Core Terminology Service</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><h3>Role</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Nigeria Core Terminology Service</strong> publishes, maintains, or provides\ncomputational access to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>CodeSystem</code>;</li>\n<li><code>ValueSet</code>;</li>\n<li><code>ConceptMap</code>;</li>\n<li><code>NamingSystem</code>, where applicable;</li>\n<li>national and program terminology; and</li>\n<li>adopted international terminology such as ICD-11, SNOMED CT, LOINC, ATC,\nand other approved systems where licensing permits.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Responsibilities</h3>\n<p>The service may:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>publish governed terminology artefacts;</li>\n<li>validate codes and ValueSet membership;</li>\n<li>expand ValueSets;</li>\n<li>provide concept lookup;</li>\n<li>translate codes using governed <code>ConceptMap</code> resources;</li>\n<li>manage terminology versions and mappings; and</li>\n<li>support terminology validation during Nigeria Core conformance testing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Supported operations may include:</p>\n<p><code>$lookup</code> | <code>$validate-code</code> | <code>$expand</code> | <code>$translate</code> | <code>$subsumes</code></p>\n<p>Availability <strong>SHALL</strong> be determined from the service <code>CapabilityStatement</code>.</p>\n<h3>Conformance expectations</h3>\n<p>A Terminology Service <strong>SHALL</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>expose valid FHIR terminology resources;</li>\n<li>preserve canonical URLs and terminology identifiers;</li>\n<li>preserve relevant terminology versions;</li>\n<li>distinguish coding systems using governed identifiers;</li>\n<li>return FHIR-conformant responses;</li>\n<li>advertise only reliably supported terminology and operations; and</li>\n<li>provide an accurate <code>CapabilityStatement</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> silently substitute terminology versions where meaning or\nvalidity could change.</p>\n<p>Where local terminology is exchanged, the original code and coding system\n<strong>SHALL</strong> be retained. Version information <strong>SHOULD</strong> be retained where\nrelevant, and governed mappings <strong>SHOULD</strong> use published <code>ConceptMap</code>\nresources.</p>\n<p>Mappings <strong>SHOULD NOT</strong> be treated as simple text substitutions. Where no valid\nmapping exists, a service <strong>SHOULD</strong> report that no translation can be\ndetermined rather than inventing a code.</p>\n<p>Required terminology bindings defined by Nigeria Core profiles <strong>SHALL</strong> be\nhonoured.</p>\n<h3>Governance and licensing</h3>\n<p>Terminology governance <strong>SHOULD</strong> address approval, versioning, retirement,\nmapping, publication, correction, and stewardship.</p>\n<p>National terminology <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> be locally modified while retaining the same\ncanonical identifier if the modification changes its governed meaning.</p>\n<p>Implementers <strong>SHALL</strong> comply with applicable licensing and distribution\nrequirements for external terminologies.</p>\n<h3>Relationships</h3>\n<p>The Terminology Service commonly supports the <strong>Nigeria Core Requestor,\nResponder, Registry Service,</strong> and <strong>Conformance and Sandbox Service</strong>.</p>\n<p>Facilities may consume shared national or subnational terminology services\nrather than operating independent terminology servers.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
